# Response headers. The directives below are HEADER-ONLY: a browser ignores
# frame-ancestors and X-Frame-Options when they appear in a <meta> tag, which is
# where the inherited index.html put them. The page looked protected against
# clickjacking and was not.
#
# connect-src carries the Supabase project and the FastAPI service on Fly
# (https://vega-api.fly.dev). The dev server adds http://localhost:8000 via its
# CSP response header so a locally running API is reachable; see
# apps/web/vite.config.ts. The page cannot call an origin this list does not
# name, and the browser refuses it silently.
#
# This file is the Netlify and Cloudflare Pages format. Fly.io needs the same
# headers set in fly.toml or by the server; whichever host is chosen in Phase 2's
# deploy step must carry these or the protection is decorative again.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://kscgvfzzzbmqohuuiiab.supabase.co wss://kscgvfzzzbmqohuuiiab.supabase.co https://vega-api.fly.dev; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
